Cell["\<\
The extra collective-mode closure assumes uniform control and atomic \
linewidths. It does not separately resolve motional sidebands, inhomogeneous \
light shifts, blockade, or additional independent standing-wave channels. The \
example Q also assumes perpendicular UV and exact matching to the chosen \
reciprocal-lattice vectors. Efficiency denotes coherent signal conversion, \
not a noise or fidelity calculation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"33c43487-bc15-b144-baeb-efa68e639b7c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Numerical example: choose parameters, then substitute Q", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2580566b-b7f6-f44a-894e-61d814ddc5d8"],

Cell["\<\
The original notebook parameter set is preserved as parmsOriginal. \
parmsScreenshot reproduces the previously supplied 82.094% screenshot (the \
exact resonance value is 82.0957%; its 1000-point grid does not sample zero). \
Select either preset below. Numerical rates are in MHz, as in the supplied \
notebook.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"42c15289-3e35-be42-bbe5-cfb8214b88c7"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gopt", "=", "0.025`"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gmm", "=", "0.091`"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Natoms", "=", 
   RowBox[{"5", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["10", "5"]}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]UV", "=", "0.03`"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]UV", "=", "1"}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[Theta]UV", "=", 
